    "title": "Franklin County man wanted for escape, PSP say - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Alton Northup ,\n1 days ago\nFRANKLIN COUNTY, Pa. (WHTM) — A Franklin County man is on the run after removing his court-ordered ankle monitor, Pennsylvania State Police said.\nTroopers said Robert Guilfoyle, 22, left his residence Monday in Hamilton Township. His roommates told police he was consuming alcohol and that a large kitchen knife was missing from the property after he left, State Police said.\nClose Thanks for signing up!\nWatch for us in your inbox.\nSubscribe Now\nBreaking News Alerts Franklin County Adult Probation contacted Guilfoyle, who said he was on foot and would not turn himself in.\nPennsylvania State Police said Robert Guilfoyle, 22, left his residence Monday in Hamilton Township, Franklin County. | Pennsylvania State Police Guilfoyle is 5 feet 11 inches, 160 pounds and has blue eyes and brown hair. His last known address is 1024 Warm Spring Road, Lot 28, in Chambersburg, police said.\nOnline court records show he was previously convicted of misdemeanor possession of drug paraphernalia. He now faces a felony escape charge.\nState Police asked anyone with information on Guilfoyle to call 911 or the State Police Chambersburg Station at (717) 264-5161.\nThis is a developing story. Stay with abc27 News as more information becomes available\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to ABC27.\n6",
